Na2CO3 solution:
Dissolve 106 g Na2CO3 in 1 liter of degassed H2O. Autoclave in sealed serum bottles
under CO2.

Cysteine and Na2S solutions:
To 50 ml of boiled and cooled distilled or deionized H2O add 5 g each of L-cysteine
hydrochloride and Na2S x 9 H2O. Adjust pH to 10 with 3N NaOH and store under N2 in a
serum bottle sealed with a butyl rubber stopper.

Titanium (III) citrate solution (Zehnder and Wuhrmann 1976):
 Titanium(III) chloride, 15% solution (Merck 808307)           5.000       ml
 Sodium citrate, 0.2M                                        50.000        ml
Neutralize pH with a saturated sodium carbonate solution and store in a serum bottle
under N2.




